                <pb facs="0553" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/1670: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-17T15:00:00+00:00">December 17, 1931—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 17—11:47 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>896. This Embassy’s 836 of December 3, noon.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d321-f1"/> No
                    reply has been made to the Italian Government’s proposals, it is understood
                    here; but the Chief of the Intelligence Office of the General Staff of the
                    Ministry of Marine, Captain Fernet, has informed the Naval Attaché of this
                    Embassy that it is the opinion of the Ministry of Marine that the proposals are
                    completely unacceptable to the French Government. Information repeated to Rome,
                    Brussels, and London.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
